menu "CYD display"

    config CYD_LCD_PCLK_MHZ
        int "SPI pixel clock (MHz)"
        range 10 80
        default 40
        help
            Start at 40 MHz. The TFT is on HSPI's IO_MUX pins, so 60-80 MHz
            may work; keep the fastest clock that is stable on your board.

    config CYD_LCD_BGR
        bool "Panel uses BGR element order"
        default n
        help
            Leave off if red and blue come out right. Turn on if they are
            swapped (some CYD batches are wired BGR).

    config CYD_LCD_INVERT_DEFAULT
        bool "Invert colours by default"
        default n
        help
            Panels vary between CYD clones. If dark scenes look bright and
            washed out, flip this. It can also be changed at runtime.

    config CYD_LCD_SWAP_XY
        bool "Swap X and Y"
        default y
        help
            On this CYD the controller's column address runs along the 320 px
            edge. Swapping gives the 240x320 portrait address space the
            firmware expects; without it the last 80 columns are never written.

    config CYD_LCD_MIRROR_X
        bool "Mirror X"
        default y
        help
            With swap and both mirrors on, (0, 0) is top-left in portrait with
            the USB port at the bottom. Flip if the image is mirrored
            left-right.

    config CYD_LCD_MIRROR_Y
        bool "Mirror Y"
        default y
        help
            Flip if the image is upside down (text reflected vertically).

    config CYD_LCD_PROBE
        bool "Log controller ID registers at boot"
        default n
        help
            Reads the LCD controller's ID registers over MISO before
            initialising the panel and logs them. Used by the diagnostic image.

endmenu
